A long poem, you asked, yet space is tight—
Two lines must hold the stars, the moon, the night.
In whispers, winds through ancient forests sweep,
While dreams in silent shadows softly sleep.
The ocean roars, its voice a timeless song,
It calls the brave, the lost, the weak, the strong.
Mountains stand tall, their peaks kissed by the sky,
A silent vow that none shall ever die.
Time flows like rivers, endless, deep, and wide,
It carries hearts where memories abide.
So here, within these lines, the world unfolds—
A tale of life, of love, of truths untold.